[size=6][b]Parachute[/b][/size]

A steerable ram-air parachute for [b]7 Days to Die v3.4 (b6)[/b], packed into your chest armor as an armor mod. Jump off something tall, press Jump in the air, and glide down with no fall damage. Works in single player, peer-hosted games and on dedicated servers.

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]One press to open:[/b] while falling, press Jump to open the canopy. Press Jump again to cut it away.
[*][b]Steerable:[/b] hold Forward to dive faster, Back to flare and slow down, Left and Right to slide sideways. The canopy glides the way you look.
[*][b]No fall damage[/b] while the canopy is open, including the touchdown.
[*][b]Reusable:[/b] the parachute is never used up. It repacks itself after every landing.
[*][b]Third-person view under the canopy:[/b] the camera pulls back behind you like a vehicle camera, then returns to your chosen view when you land.
[*][b]Worn pack:[/b] a parachute pack shows on your back while the mod is installed, and the riser straps run from it when the canopy opens.
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] other players see your canopy open, steer and collapse, hear it from where you are, and see your pack.
[*][b]Configurable:[/b] speeds, controls, camera and pack placement are all in [font=Courier New]ParachuteConfig.json[/font].
[/list]

[size=5][b]Getting one[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Craft it[/b] at a workbench once you know the recipe: 80 cloth, 10 leather, 3 duct tape, 1 sewing kit and 4 mechanical parts.
[*][b]Learn the recipe[/b] from the [i]Parachute Mod Schematic[/i], found as loot with the other tier-2 mod schematics or bought from a trader.
[*][b]Buy it[/b] from traders, who sometimes stock it with their other armor mods.
[/list]
Install the Parachute Mod in the [b]chest armor[/b] you are wearing.

[size=5][b]Controls[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Jump (in the air):[/b] open the canopy; press again to cut away
[*][b]Forward:[/b] dive, faster forward and down
[*][b]Back:[/b] flare, slower forward and down
[*][b]Left / Right:[/b] slide sideways
[*][b]Mouse:[/b] steer
[/list]
[list]
[*]The canopy needs at least 3 m of clear air below you to open. The Jump that leaves the ground never opens it.
[*]It won't open in water, on a ladder, in a vehicle or while wearing a jetpack.
[*]It stows itself when you land, enter water, grab a ladder or get in a vehicle.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Unzip into the game's [font=Courier New]Mods[/font] folder so you have [font=Courier New]Mods\Parachute\ModInfo.xml[/font].
[*]Keep [font=Courier New]Mods\0_TFP_Harmony[/font], which comes with the game.
[*]Start the game with [b]Easy Anti-Cheat off[/b].
[/list]

[size=4][b]Multiplayer[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Install the mod on the [b]server and every player's game[/b].
[*][b]Dedicated server:[/b] put it in the server's [font=Courier New]Mods[/font] folder and set [font=Courier New]EACEnabled[/font] to [font=Courier New]false[/font] in [font=Courier New]serverconfig.xml[/font].
[*][b]Peer-hosted:[/b] the host and every player who joins install it and play with EAC off.
[*]A player who joins without the mod isn't kicked, but can't open a canopy and won't see anyone else's.
[*]Each player's [font=Courier New]ParachuteConfig.json[/font] applies only to their own game.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Made for [b]v3.4 (b6)[/b]. For v3.3 use Parachute 0.6.4.
[*]Works alongside the Grappling Hook mod. The Jump press that lets go of a rope doesn't open the canopy.
[*]Uses Harmony patches on player movement, fall damage and the camera, so other mods that change those may conflict.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Known issues[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]One pack placement doesn't fit every armor: with some outfits the straps sink into the clothing, and armor with its own backpack can clash with the pack.
[*]Other players' canopies lean and tilt from an estimate of how they move, so it can lag slightly behind what they see.
[*]Another player's canopy collapses about half a second after they land.
[*]The deploy sound will be revisited.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Version[/b][/size]
1.0.0-beta (the game shows 1.0.0).
